---
import { SITE } from '../config';

/**
 * Shown at the foot of every article.
 *
 * States plainly how the piece was made and invites correction. This is a trust
 * signal, and it is also the honest position: AI-assisted drafting with human
 * review reduces errors but does not eliminate them, and readers deserve to
 * know that before they act on anything here.
 */
const email = SITE.author.email;
---

<aside class="ai-note" aria-labelledby="ai-note-heading">
  <h2 class="ai-note__title" id="ai-note-heading">How this article was made</h2>
  <p>
    This article was <strong>drafted with AI assistance and reviewed by a person</strong>
    before publishing. A human editor checked the claims that matter, removed what could
    not be supported, and decided it was worth publishing.
  </p>
  <p>
    That process reduces mistakes but does not remove them. Prices, features and policies
    also change after publication. Treat this as general information, not professional
    advice — and check anything you intend to rely on.
  </p>
  <p class="ai-note__cta">
    <strong>Spotted something wrong?</strong> Tell us and we will fix it — corrections are
    made promptly and the update date at the top of the article changes so readers can see
    it was revised. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or use the
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .ai-note {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding: var(--space-m);
    background-color: var(--bg-sunken);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .ai-note__title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .ai-note p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .ai-note__cta {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
